Done. Google's bad-key reply now gets the auth hint (commit 07b24627, Fixes #1163).

What was wrong: Google answers a bad key with 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT and "reason": "API_KEY_INVALID", not a 401. The check in diagnose_api_error_for only recognised 401, unauthorized, invalid api key, invalid_api_key and authentication, so the user got raw JSON and "Exiting." with no hint.

Dependency check: I looked at yoagent 0.27.5 first. Its ProviderError::classify only treats 401 and 403 as auth errors, so Google's 400 arrives as a general API error. There was nothing upstream to reuse, so the check lives in yoyo.

Changes:
• `src/prompt_retry.rs`:
  • The auth check now also matches api_key_invalid or api key not valid (lowercased). It never matches a bare 400 or invalid_argument, because those also cover ordinary bad requests.
  • When yoyo sends a key from another provider's variable, the hint now lists every variable the provider reads: "Neither GEMINI_API_KEY nor GOOGLE_API_KEY is set…". Before, it named only GOOGLE_API_KEY, though yoyo reads GEMINI_API_KEY first. Providers with a single key variable get the same text as before.
• `src/prompt_retry_auth_tests.rs`: 4 new tests, all of which failed before the fix:
  • Google's real response body, with the source quoted in the doc comment, gets the auth hint.
  • Each of the two Google markers on its own triggers it.
  • A Google 400 about a misspelled field does not get the auth hint. This one passed before the fix too, which is what it's for.
  • The full hint text is checked, and so is the advice: the variable it tells you to export is one yoyo actually reads for Google, and both Google variables are named.
• Docs: one line in common-issues.md. tests/module_size.rs raises the size limit for prompt_retry.rs from 2793 to 2803 lines (+10).

Checks: build, clippy with -D warnings and fmt all pass. Tests: 7374 passed, 0 failed. I also ran the exact failing command with the built binary against Google's real endpoint (no Gemini key, Anthropic key set). It now prints the hint before exiting, and the output is in the commit message.

Not done:
• I only tested Google. I didn't add bad-key strings for other providers from memory. The 11 providers I haven't checked are listed on #1163.
• When no key is set at all, the Google hint still says only "GOOGLE_API_KEY is not set." That's true, but it doesn't mention GEMINI_API_KEY, which yoyo reads first. I noted this on #1163, but this commit closes #1163 when it's pushed, so nothing open tracks it. It needs its own issue if it's worth fixing.
